      "composition": "single-ornament",
      "description": "A large horizontal engraved panel filled edge to edge with curling acanthus stems and lobed leaves. At the top centre a seated couple, a woman in a tall hennin with a small dog on her lap and a young man in a cap, under a banderole inscribed with the artist's name. Among the scrolls are two birds at the top corners, nude figures climbing and riding the stems, a bearded man with a spear at the right, a youth rising from a tuft of grass at the bottom, a fox at the lower left, a man raising a cup at the lower right and two hanging pod finials. Dark brown ink on cream, background transparent.",
